<attribute name="presentationName" nodeId="e8c4dc9f">Prepare for the sprint review</attribute>
<attribute name="briefDescription" nodeId="6d5d76c2"></attribute>
<attribute name="suppressed" nodeId="5dc20dc6">false</attribute>
<attribute name="orderingGuide" nodeId="d171af98"></attribute>
<attribute name="authors" nodeId="78a1028"></attribute>
<attribute name="changeDate" nodeId="23e982f0"></attribute>
<attribute name="changeDescription" nodeId="f3b59199"></attribute>
<attribute name="version" nodeId="b6e475b7"></attribute>
<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="20917146"></attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="d4875a42"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="6bfea6a9">&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        The Product Owner and appropriate stakeholders should understand each Backlog Item, its acceptance criteria and
        purpose so they can ask meaningful questions and be ready to discuss the Product Backlog as it currently stands
        (including a review of the next highest priority items) during the sprint review.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        The goal of the sprint review is to agree on the best course of action for subsequent sprints, making it an
        opportunity to both learn and adapt. Therefore, preparing for the sprint review is crucial to confirm the learning
        and adaptation is as successful as possible.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        When booking a room for the sprint review, consider an environment that will make participants feel comfortable and
        invite candor thereby driving a more interactive and productive discussion.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Remind the team before sprint planning that there will be a sprint review at the end of each sprint and describe
        what to expect.
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="b9682e1b"></attribute>
<attribute name="usageGuidance" nodeId="e06d20b6"></attribute>
<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="ce6eecd5">&lt;p&gt;
    Prepare for the sprint review by:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Confirming progress
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Developing a plan
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Communicating purpose
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Coordinating administrative tasks
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Confirm progress by having the team identify which Backlog Items are already complete or will most likely be completed
    by the end of the sprint. Highlight any incomplete Backlog Items and prepare a supporting justification for the
    stakeholders. Based on the progress of complete versus incomplete Backlog Items for the sprint, determine whether the
    sprint goal was met.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Based on these findings, plan which Backlog Items to present out of those completed. The team will determine which
    Backlog Items to present and decide on the best manner in which to present each item. Use this information to
    create&amp;nbsp;a sprint review agenda that allows enough time for each presentation.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    The Development Team should discuss all difficulties and successes encountered during the current sprint. Based on the
    discussion, determine which topics should be brought to the broader group during the sprint review so as to focus on
    only the most pressing items.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Prior to the sprint review it is imperative for the Product Owner, as the primary person responsible for stakeholder
    management, to communicate the purpose of the meeting to all participants in advance. Explain that the sprint review is
    intended to be a collaborative working session and not a one-sided demonstration. This is so that&amp;nbsp;all the
    participants are on the same page and will allow the meeting to flow more easily if everyone understands the structure
    ahead of time.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Finally, coordinate all administrative tasks which may include:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Booking a room
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Sending meeting invites
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Gathering any necessary supplies (flipchart, visual aids, etc.)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Confirming attendance
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Distributing meeting materials, if any, in advance of the meeting
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
</Element>
